# Read API (backend/api)

# Path to the content Git repository the API reads and writes (change-set branches). Use a bare
# repository (`git clone --bare`): the API never moves a branch checked out in a working tree.
CCMS_CONTENT_DIR=/path/to/content-repo
# Machine clients authenticate with their service account's own token ("Authorization: Bearer
# ccms_sat_..."), issued in Admin or by `POST /service-accounts/{id}/tokens`; the first one of a
# deployment with `pnpm nx run api:service-token -- <account> --role <role>` (printed once).
# Optional: a shared secret, for local use and demo mode only (required in demo mode). Unset (the
# default), only service accounts' tokens authenticate; leave it empty in a deployment. At least 32
# characters; generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32. `pnpm nx run api:setup-local` writes one.
# Refused with sign-in (CCMS_OIDC_ISSUER), but for a loopback issuer in local runs and tests.
CCMS_API_TOKEN=
# Who a request with the shared token acts as: token or demo (default: token).
# token: the shared token (when set) acts as a read-only service (reads every ref, drafts included,
#   changes nothing; the server warns at start-up); an X-Ccms-User header is refused (400).
# demo: the token is still required, and an "X-Ccms-User: <user ID>" header picks a seeded user
#   (`pnpm nx run api:db-seed -- --example`) to act as. Anyone with the token can then act as any
#   user, the admin included: for demonstrations only, never where real people sign in. The server
#   warns at start-up. The editor's sign-in page lists the seeded users in demo mode; in token mode it
#   says sign-in is not set up. `pnpm nx run api:setup-local` writes demo (when unset) and seeds the
#   example users into an empty local database.
CCMS_AUTH_MODE=
# Failed authentications (a missing, wrong, revoked or expired token) one client address may make
# per window before its requests are refused with 429 too-many-failed-attempts and Retry-After,
# until the window ends (a valid service account token still acts). Whole number, 0 = no limit
# (default: 20). Counted per server, in memory, by the connection's address: behind a reverse proxy
# all clients share the proxy's, so raise the limit there or set 0.
CCMS_AUTH_FAILURES_MAX=
# The window of CCMS_AUTH_FAILURES_MAX, in milliseconds, 1000 to 86400000 (default: 60000).
CCMS_AUTH_FAILURES_WINDOW_MS=

# Sign-in with OpenID Connect (#37; backend/api/README.md, "Sign-in"): people sign in to the editor at any
# OpenID Connect provider, found by discovery (<issuer>/.well-known/openid-configuration). Off unless
# CCMS_OIDC_ISSUER is set; cannot be on with CCMS_AUTH_MODE=demo (the server refuses to start). Service
# accounts keep their own tokens. Register the client at the provider with the redirect URL below and, for
# signing out there too, the post-logout redirect URL <CCMS_EDITOR_URL>sign-in.
# The provider's issuer, exactly as its discovery document names it, e.g. https://id.example.org/docs.
# https, or http only on a loopback host (a local test provider).
CCMS_OIDC_ISSUER=
# The client ID the provider gave this deployment. Required with CCMS_OIDC_ISSUER.
CCMS_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# The client's secret (client_secret_basic). Unset: a public client, signing in with PKCE only. In a container,
# CCMS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE may name a file holding it instead (a Compose secret; "Secrets from files" below).
CCMS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Where the provider sends the browser back: the editor's address plus api/auth/oidc/callback, e.g.
# https://docs.example.org/api/auth/oidc/callback. Required with CCMS_OIDC_ISSUER; on the editor's origin
# (the session cookie is the editor's), https or http on loopback only.
CCMS_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL=
# The scopes asked for, space-separated; must include openid (default: openid profile email).
CCMS_OIDC_SCOPES=
# Whether a first sign-in joins an existing user whose email address the provider reports as verified
# (email_verified): pending, off or any (default: pending).
# pending: only a user who has never signed in with any provider: one an admin created or the seed wrote (the
#   first admin), waiting for their first sign-in. Recorded as user.identity-link.
# any: any user without an identity at this issuer yet, also one who signs in elsewhere. Only for a provider that
#   guarantees nobody can set an address they do not own and have it reported verified: otherwise whoever sets
#   someone's address takes over their account here.
# off: never; every first sign-in makes a new user (give roles by group or by hand afterwards).
# With pending or any, the provider must not let people set an email address it then reports as verified.
CCMS_OIDC_LINK_BY_EMAIL=
# The claim the provider sends a person's groups in (ID token or userinfo): a name, or a dotted path into
# nested claims, e.g. org.groups (default: groups). Groups give roles through the group mappings
# (Admin, or POST /group-mappings); roles assigned directly stay.
CCMS_OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=
# What the editor's sign-in button names, e.g. Company ID: at most 60 characters. Unset: a neutral wording.
CCMS_OIDC_NAME=
# The editor's address, ending in /, e.g. https://docs.example.org/: where a sign-in comes back to and the
# origin a signed-in change must come from. Default: the origin of CCMS_OIDC_REDIRECT_URL plus /.
CCMS_EDITOR_URL=
# A session ends after this many minutes without a request, 5 to 43200 (default: 480, 8 hours).
CCMS_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES=
# A session ends this many hours after signing in, whatever its use, 1 to 8760 (default: 168, 7 days).
CCMS_SESSION_MAX_HOURS=
# Signing in with an email address and a password (#610; backend/api/README.md, "Sign-in"): on or off
# (default: on, except with CCMS_AUTH_MODE=demo, where it is off and on is refused). Off: only OpenID Connect,
# codes by email (only if CCMS_EMAIL_CODE_SIGN_IN=on says so) and tokens. Admins invite people
# (Admin > Users); a one-time link sets the first password. The first admin:
# `pnpm nx run api:first-admin -- <email>` (deploy/README.md). "Forgot password" shows when email
# (CCMS_MAIL_URL) and CCMS_PUBLIC_URL are set, for people who have a password. Failed sign-ins count toward
# CCMS_AUTH_FAILURES_MAX per client address and CCMS_PASSWORD_FAILURES_MAX per account. Turning it off stops
# the password sessions. Sessions, sign-out and their limits are the ones above.
CCMS_PASSWORD_SIGN_IN=
# How many days an invite link works, 1 to 90 (default: 7). A reset link works one hour.
CCMS_INVITE_DAYS=
# The first admin (#373): an email address, made with the role "admin" (every permission) when the API
# starts on an instance without users, and ignored from then on (default: unset, none; or run first-admin,
# deploy/README.md, "Quick start"). With password sign-in on, a one-time link to choose their password is
# printed in the API's log (valid one hour, once, closed too by their first sign-in with a provider or by a code by email; the base is
# CCMS_PUBLIC_URL, else CCMS_EDITOR_URL). With OpenID Connect, they sign in with the provider, which finds the
# user by this verified address. With codes by email alone (#639), they sign in with "Email me a code" at this
# address (no link is printed).
CCMS_FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# Whether that first start prints the link in the log, true or false (default: true). false: no link is made;
# print one with first-admin on the command line, which never goes to the log.
CCMS_FIRST_ADMIN_LINK_LOG=
# The first admin's display name, 1 to 200 characters (default: the address's part before the "@").
CCMS_FIRST_ADMIN_NAME=
# Failed password checks one email address may have per window before it is refused (429), 0 to 1000000
# (default: 10; 0: no limit); "Forgot password" requests for it count apart, under the same limit. Apart from
# CCMS_AUTH_FAILURES_MAX, so it holds behind a shared address too. Kept in the database, shared by every server.
CCMS_PASSWORD_FAILURES_MAX=
# The window of CCMS_PASSWORD_FAILURES_MAX, in milliseconds, 1000 to 86400000 (default: 900000, 15 minutes).
CCMS_PASSWORD_FAILURES_WINDOW_MS=
# Signing in with a one-time code by email (#634; backend/api/README.md, "Sign-in"), beside passwords and
# OpenID Connect or alone (#639): on or off. Default: on wherever email is set up (CCMS_MAIL_URL, and the
# secret key it needs) and password sign-in is on, off otherwise; never in demo mode (on is refused there).
# With CCMS_PASSWORD_SIGN_IN=off, only an explicit on offers it: beside the provider (a way in that does not
# pass through the provider), or as the only way to sign in, with no provider. on needs CCMS_MAIL_URL (refused
# at start-up without it). The sign-in page then offers "Email me a code": a six-digit code and a link that signs in
# (the link only with CCMS_PUBLIC_URL), once, for CCMS_EMAIL_CODE_MINUTES. Requests and wrong codes each count
# per account under CCMS_PASSWORD_FAILURES_MAX (apart from passwords and from each other) and per client
# address under CCMS_AUTH_FAILURES_MAX; once the wrong codes use up the account's tries, the code is revoked.
# Turning it off ends the sessions begun with a code.
CCMS_EMAIL_CODE_SIGN_IN=
# How many minutes a code by email and its link work, 1 to 60 (default: 10).
CCMS_EMAIL_CODE_MINUTES=
# Branch, tag or commit used when a request has no ?ref= (default: HEAD).
CCMS_DEFAULT_REF=main
# CCMS_CONTENT_CACHE_MB: how much parsed content (modules, manifests, terms, translation records) one
# server keeps in memory, in MiB of the files' text; parsed, it takes five to six times that. A file is
# parsed once however many commits hold it, and listing every module (search, media, translation
# status) reads them all, so keep it above the text of every file at the commits read most
# (`git ls-tree -r -l main`), or each listing parses them again. Whole number from 1 to 16384
# (default: 64, about 30,000 module files and 350 MiB in memory).
CCMS_CONTENT_CACHE_MB=
# CCMS_CONTENT_INDEX_CACHE_MB: how much memory the content's indexes take at most, in MiB, estimated from their
# strings (#552): blob IDs by path and by folder, the files two commits differ by, file histories, deleted files,
# folder listings and the module listings per commit, each a fixed share of it; the newest index of each whole
# folder is kept however large, beside the rest. On top of CCMS_CONTENT_CACHE_MB and of the 64 MiB of file contents kept. This bounds the content's
# reader; the API's few other Git readers (change sets, change feed, releases) keep small caches of their own,
# 32 MiB each at most (in practice only changed-file lists). The default holds about 50,000 module files' paths. Raise it when history, change and media reads of a large repository slow
# down. Whole number from 1 to 4096 (default: 32).
CCMS_CONTENT_INDEX_CACHE_MB=
# CCMS_SEARCH_INDEXES: how many search indexes one server keeps, one per commit and reading scope
# (readers who may see the same share one), with the rankings of their recent searches; the least
# recently used goes. Unchanged modules' text is shared between them. Whole number from 1 to 1024
# (default: 16).
CCMS_SEARCH_INDEXES=
# Search (#54; backend/api/README.md, "Search"). CCMS_SEARCH_ADAPTER: postgres (default) indexes the content in
# the database: words in any of their forms in the content's language, typos in titles and keywords (pg_trgm,
# created by the migrations), and every word anywhere in a field as the in-memory search finds it; the index is
# derived data, made as readers search (a commit once, a later commit only what changed). memory: word matching
# alone, in each server's memory, rebuilt per commit and reading scope (small installs, no stemming or typos).
CCMS_SEARCH_ADAPTER=
# The search's limits (#539; backend/api/README.md, "Postgres search"). Each server counts its own: behind a load
# balancer with N servers a reader gets up to N times CCMS_SEARCH_PER_MINUTE.
# CCMS_SEARCH_PER_MINUTE: searches (GET /search, every page counts) one reader, a person or a service account, may
# ask for per minute on each server; past it 429 rate-limited with Retry-After. It also bounds the embedder calls a
# reader's queries make. At most 2 of a reader's searches are in progress at once (another is 429 too). Whole number 1-6000
# (default: 120; the editor's palette asks at most about 5 a second while someone types).
CCMS_SEARCH_PER_MINUTE=
# CCMS_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_MS: the most time one search may spend in the database, all of its statements together
# (each also stops after 5 s); past it 503 database-timeout with Retry-After, and the connection is free again.
# Writing a commit's index the first time it is searched is not counted. Postgres search only. Milliseconds,
# 100-60000 (default: 5000).
CCMS_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_MS=
# CCMS_SEARCH_CONCURRENCY: searches one server runs in the database at once; more wait up to 2 s for their turn (at
# most 4 waiting per search running), then 503 search-busy with Retry-After. Keep it well under
# CCMS_DATABASE_POOL_MAX, so searches never hold the whole pool. Postgres search only. Whole number 1-100 (default: 4).
CCMS_SEARCH_CONCURRENCY=
# The search index's sweep (#540; backend/api/README.md, "Postgres search"): every hour, on each server that runs
# background work (CCMS_ROLE all or worker), bounded per run. Postgres search only.
# CCMS_SEARCH_SWEEP_AFTER_DAYS: the grace period. A commit's index (scope) no reader searched for this long is
# dropped, then the documents no scope names that are as old, then the texts (what is embedded) no document has used
# for this long, with their embeddings of every model. So the text of a deleted draft, or of content changed since an
# old commit, is gone at most about twice this long after it was last searched. Whole number of days 1-365 (default: 7).
CCMS_SEARCH_SWEEP_AFTER_DAYS=
# CCMS_SEARCH_MODEL_KEPT_DAYS: how long the embeddings of a model no server has configured any more (CCMS_EMBEDDER_MODEL
# changed, or the embedder turned off) are kept, so switching back within it embeds nothing again; then the sweep drops
# them, and logs it. Whole number of days 1-365 (default: 7).
# Not a setting: `pnpm nx run api:index-rebuild -- --drop-embeddings` also drops every embedding (and the texts),
# so everything searched afterwards is embedded again, sent to the embedder again (and paid for again, with a hosted one).
CCMS_SEARCH_MODEL_KEPT_DAYS=
# Semantic search (meaning): an embeddings endpoint, off by default. Unset, nothing is sent anywhere and search is
# full text plus typos. WHEN SET, MODULE TEXT LEAVES THE SERVER: a background job (search.embed) posts every
# indexed text (titles, keywords, block and FAQ text of what readers searched, drafts included for their authors)
# and each search posts its query to this URL. Point it at a model you run yourself (beside the API) unless you
# accept that content goes to a hosted provider. Any endpoint that takes {"model", "input": [texts]} and answers
# {"data": [{"embedding": [numbers], "index"}]}: the full URL a request is posted to (http:// or https://, no
# credentials, query or fragment; https:// required with an API key, except to localhost). Needs
# CCMS_SEARCH_ADAPTER=postgres and pgvector in the database (deploy/README.md, "Semantic search").
CCMS_EMBEDDER_URL=
# Sent as "Authorization: Bearer <key>"; optional (a model you run yourself may need none). Never logged.
# Or CCMS_EMBEDDER_API_KEY_FILE (below).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_API_KEY=
# The model name the endpoint expects (the request's "model"); required with CCMS_EMBEDDER_URL. Vectors are
# kept per model and dimensions: changing either embeds everything again.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_MODEL=
# How many numbers the model's vectors have (e.g. 384); required with CCMS_EMBEDDER_URL. Whole number 1-2000.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_DIMENSIONS=
# How long one request to the endpoint may take in milliseconds (a search then goes on without meaning; the job
# retries); range 100-120000 (default: 10000).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_TIMEOUT_MS=
# How close a block's meaning has to be to the query's to be found by meaning alone: cosine similarity in percent,
# 0-100 (default: 50). Depends on the model: raise it if unrelated results show up, lower it if paraphrases are
# missed.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_MIN_SIMILARITY=
# Origins allowed to show the HTML previews (GET /modules/:lang/:id/preview, GET /manuals/:id/variants/:variant/:lang/html)
# in a frame, comma-separated: scheme, host and optional port only, e.g. https://editor.example.com,http://localhost:4200.
# Sent as the previews' CSP frame-ancestors, next to 'self' (a dev server that proxies the API is 'self'). Default: none.
CCMS_EDITOR_ORIGINS=
# Where this deployment's source code can be downloaded: an http:// or https:// URL without credentials, e.g. the
# repository of the version you run. The software is AGPL-3.0-only, whose section 13 asks a modified version run as
# a network service to offer its users its source; GET /about hands the URL to clients and the editor links to it
# (account menu, sign-in page). Default: none; the editor then shows the licence only, and Admin → System asks the
# admin to set it. Set it whenever you run a modified version.
CCMS_SOURCE_URL=
# Where readers reach this deployment (#450): the base of every manual's stable address
# (<url>/d/<product>/<manual>/<variant>/<lang>, the latest release; @<revision> after the language for one
# release) and of the QR codes made of them, for print. An http:// or https:// URL without credentials, query or
# fragment (a trailing / is added; a path is kept, e.g. https://docs.example.com/manuals/). The editor's web server
# serves /d/ from the API (deploy/README.md). Default: none; the editor then shows the addresses as paths, and QR
# codes (and the QR code a release's PDF can print, openfolia.yaml delivery.pdfQrCode) are not made. Who may open an
# address is the content's configuration, openfolia.yaml delivery.access (public, signed-in by default, or off).
CCMS_PUBLIC_URL=
# The most a project's openfolia.yaml delivery.access may open its stable addresses on this deployment (#553): public
# (no cap), signed-in (a reader with a token) or off (no address opens). A project asking for more is served at
# this, its PDFs print no QR code unless it is public, and each manual's checks report delivery-access-capped.
# Default: public.
CCMS_DELIVERY_MAX_ACCESS=
# The query parameters a stable address ignores (#553), so a link shared with tracking parameters still opens; any
# other parameter a route does not take stays a 400. Comma-separated, each a parameter name or a prefix ending in *
# (letters, digits, _ . -; a bare * is refused), or none. Matched case-sensitively, never dropping a parameter the
# route takes (theme). E.g. utm_*,ref_*,<your click-ID parameters>. Default: utm_*.
CCMS_DELIVERY_IGNORED_QUERY=
# How long a shared cache (a proxy, a CDN) may keep a public stable address's image before it must ask again, in
# seconds (#552): Cache-Control s-maxage with proxy-revalidate. After a release is withdrawn its images can stay in
# a shared cache this long; a reader's own browser keeps an image a day. Lower: a withdrawal reaches caches sooner,
# more revalidations (each a cheap 304); 0: every request is revalidated. Whole number from 0 to 86400 (default: 300).
CCMS_DELIVERY_SHARED_MAX_AGE=
# What identifies this build of the API (#552), e.g. the commit or image tag it was built from: 1 to 128 of
# A-Za-z0-9._:+-. A stable address page's ETag is known before rendering, from the release, the reader, the theme
# and this, so a revalidation is a 304 without rendering. Set it to the same value on every server of one build, and
# to a new one with each build, so the servers' ETags agree and a new build's pages replace the old. Default: none,
# then each process makes its own (a restart renders each page once again). Never keep one value across builds: caches
# would keep the old build's pages.
CCMS_BUILD_ID=
# Which proxies in front of the API to believe about the client's address (X-Forwarded-For), for the limits keyed by
# it: /d/'s rate limit (CCMS_DELIVERY_PER_MINUTE) and failed authentications. none (the default): trust no proxy, the
# client is the connection's address and a forged header changes nothing. A hop count from 1 to 10 trusts that many
# proxies nearest the API, whoever they are: only where no client can reach the API but through them. Otherwise
# comma-separated IP addresses, subnets (172.16.0.0/12, fd00::/16; at least a /8, an IPv6 one a /16) or loopback, linklocal, uniquelocal (the private
# ranges). true (any client could name any address) is refused. The container setup: deploy/README.md, "Reverse proxy
# with TLS".
CCMS_TRUST_PROXY=
# Pages, PDFs and QR codes one client may ask for under /d/ per minute, on each server: a request without a token by
# its address (see CCMS_TRUST_PROXY), one with a token by its actor. Past it, 429 rate-limited with Retry-After. A 304
# revalidation of a page or a PDF counts nothing, nor do a page's images, stylesheets and fonts. 0 to 6000, 0 for no
# limit (default: 60). Raise it where many readers share one address (a site behind one NAT).
CCMS_DELIVERY_PER_MINUTE=
# Where the user guide is (the docs site, or a copy of it): every editor screen's help link, the account menu's
# "Help for this page", the search palette's Help group and the "Learn more" links open a page under it, in the UI
# language (guide/writing/content-browser, after de/ in German; each screen names its page by article ID, from the
# guide index the editor's build ships with the guide of its version). GET /about hands it to clients. An http://
# or https:// URL without credentials (a trailing / is added; a sub-path such as https://intranet.example/docs/ is
# kept), or off for no such links (an offline instance). Default: https://docs.openfolia.com/.
CCMS_DOCS_URL=
# How release tags (annotated, immutable) are named. {product} and {revision} are each filled in once, as a
# whole path component; the rest may hold only A-Za-z0-9._/- (default: release/{product}/{revision}).
CCMS_RELEASE_TAG=
# How maintenance lines' branches are named (POST /maintenance-lines, one per older product revision being fixed).
# {product} and {revision} (the base release's) are each filled in once, as a whole path component; the rest may hold
# only A-Za-z0-9._/- and must not start with change-sets/ or refs/, nor equal CCMS_RELEASE_TAG
# (default: maintenance/{product}/{revision}).
CCMS_MAINTENANCE_BRANCH=
# Address and port to listen on (port 0 = any free port). Defaults to 127.0.0.1:3100; set HOST=0.0.0.0 only behind TLS.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=3100
# What this process does (#527); the same image and code for each. One of:
#   all     (default) everything in one process: the API, the background jobs and loops, the PDF pool.
#   api     serves the API and enqueues jobs; consumes none, runs no background loop (sweeps, outbox
#           consumers, recounts), and keeps a small PDF pool (CCMS_PDF_WORKERS, default 2) for what readers
#           ask for (a manual's PDF, page images, checks). Its /health/ready never depends on a worker.
#   worker  consumes every job (release planning and files, imports, webhook deliveries, ...) and runs the
#           background loops and the PDF pool; serves no HTTP but GET /health and /health/ready on HOST:PORT
#           (with the job queue's counts: keep HOST=127.0.0.1 unless a probe outside needs it), and never
#           migrates: it waits up to 120 s for the API's migrations. Several workers plan a product's releases
#           one at a time (a Postgres advisory lock, held on one connection of its own beside the pool while a
#           release is planned; like migrating, it needs a direct connection or a session-mode pooler).
#   backup  the backup service (#529; the backup image sets it): the arguments are its command (run, now, list,
#           restore ...), no API and no jobs.
# Run any number of workers beside the API instances (deploy/README.md, "Workers").
CCMS_ROLE=
# A worker's CPU priority: the nice value it takes at start, which its PDF worker processes inherit, so on a host
# shared with the API its renders yield the CPU to the API's readers. Whole number 0 (normal) to 19 (lowest);
# default: 10. Only raised: a process already started at a higher nice value keeps it. Ignored by other roles.
CCMS_WORKER_NICE=

# Postgres for operational state (users, roles, locks, the audit log); compose.yaml runs version 18.
# Required. Format: postgres://user:password@host:5432/database (postgresql:// works too; add
# ?sslmode=verify-full for TLS; node-postgres verifies the certificate for `require` too, so a private
# CA needs NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS). A Unix socket: postgres:///database?host=/socket/folder&user=name.
# Locally: `docker compose up -d`; setup-local writes this checkout's value.
CCMS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://ccms:ccms@127.0.0.1:5432/ccms
# Apply pending migrations on start: true or false (default: true). Set false when a deployment
# runs `node backend/api/dist/database/migrate.main.js` (or `pnpm nx run api:db-migrate`) itself.
CCMS_DATABASE_MIGRATE=
# Most connections in the server's database pool; whole number 1-500 (default: 10). While queries wait for a
# free connection, GET /health/ready answers 503.
CCMS_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=
# How long a migration statement waits for a table lock, in milliseconds, 1-600000 (default: 10000). Past it that
# attempt rolls back (a long transaction on a migrated table makes a statement queue every later query on it).
CCMS_DATABASE_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Runs of a migration that keeps hitting that timeout before start-up fails, with 1 s, 2 s, 4 s ... pauses between
# them; whole number 1-20 (default: 3). Other failures are never repeated.
CCMS_DATABASE_MIGRATE_ATTEMPTS=
# Write transactions that hold rows others wait for (a save point, abandoning a change set, breaking locks) wait at
# most this long for a row or table lock, in milliseconds, 1-600000 (default: 5000; SET LOCAL lock_timeout). Past it the
# request rolls back and answers 503 database-timeout with Retry-After, never a 500.
CCMS_DATABASE_WRITE_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=
# How long one statement of such a transaction may run, in milliseconds, 1-600000 (default: 30000; SET LOCAL
# statement_timeout). Past it: the same 503 database-timeout.
CCMS_DATABASE_WRITE_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Tests only (backend/api): a Postgres server for the specs PGlite cannot run (concurrent transactions:
# src/change-sets/repos/lock-contention.postgres.spec.ts, save-points.postgres.spec.ts and
# src/access/repos/email-code-ways-in.postgres.spec.ts). Format as
# CCMS_DATABASE_URL, e.g. the compose one, postgres://ccms:ccms@127.0.0.1:5432/ccms; the user must be allowed to
# create databases (each run creates and drops a ccms_test_* database of its own). Unset (the default): those specs are skipped.
# The slot tooling's test (scripts/__tests__/slot-databases.test.ts) reads it too: it creates and drops three
# databases of made-up slots with random names (ccms_zz_db…, ccms_perf_zz_db…) to check `pnpm slot remove`'s drop.
CCMS_TEST_PG_URL=

# Blob store: binary files (images, later attachments and downloads) by their SHA-256, never in Git.
# Which adapter: s3 (any S3-compatible service) or fs (a folder on this machine). Required; no default.
# Locally setup-local writes s3 with the compose service (compose.yaml, SeaweedFS on 127.0.0.1:8333).
CCMS_BLOB_DRIVER=
# fs only, and then required: absolute path of the folder holding the blobs (created when missing);
# one machine only, back it up with the database.
CCMS_BLOB_FS_ROOT=
# s3 only. The service's address, http:// or https:// without credentials in it, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8333
# (unset, the default: AWS S3 itself, by region).
CCMS_S3_ENDPOINT=
# s3 only. The region (default: us-east-1; most S3-compatible services accept any).
CCMS_S3_REGION=
# s3 only, and then required: the bucket, 3-63 lowercase letters, digits, dots and dashes. It must exist; keep it
# private (the API serves images itself, never by a bucket URL). setup-local makes ccms (main checkout) or
# ccms-<slot> (an agent slot).
CCMS_S3_BUCKET=
# s3 only. Access key ID and secret, both or neither (default: neither, so the SDK's own chain applies: AWS_*
# environment variables, shared credential files, an instance or task role). Needs s3:GetObject, s3:PutObject,
# s3:DeleteObject on the bucket's objects and s3:ListBucket on the bucket (HeadBucket, for readiness).
CCMS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CCMS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# s3 only. true for path-style URLs (<endpoint>/<bucket>/<key>), which most self-hosted services need;
# true or false (default: false, virtual-hosted style as AWS uses).
CCMS_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=

# Image uploads (POST /change-sets/:id/assets) and translation imports (POST /translations/imports: the
# XLIFF file, or a ZIP of them, packed and unpacked): the largest file taken, in bytes; a larger one is 422
# too-large, and reading the request stops there. Whole number from 1 to 1073741824 (default: 10485760, 10 MiB).
CCMS_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=

# Attachments (POST /change-sets/:id/assets?kind=attachment): files of any type readers download from a module.
# The largest file stored, in bytes; a larger one is 422 too-large and reading stops there.
# Whole number from 1 to 1073741824 (default: 52428800, 50 MiB).
CCMS_MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES=
# Fonts for page designs (POST /change-sets/:id/assets?kind=font: TrueType, OpenType, WOFF or WOFF2, told by
# their bytes). The largest font stored, in bytes; a larger one is 422 too-large and reading stops there. A font
# is read whole into memory to be checked. Whole number from 1 to 67108864 (default: 10485760, 10 MiB).
CCMS_MAX_FONT_BYTES=
# Which attachment types are taken. Each is a comma-separated list of lowercase entries: a media type
# (application/zip), a top-level type (text/*) or an extension with its dot (.zip). The type is the server's,
# from the bytes and the file name (never the client's Content-Type). Dangerous types (HTML, SVG, executables,
# installers, scripts: backend/api/README.md, "Attachments") are always refused unless OPEN names them.
# ALLOW: when set, only files whose type or extension it names, at least one (default: unset, any type).
CCMS_ATTACHMENT_TYPES_ALLOW=
# DENY: refused on top of the dangerous types (default: empty).
CCMS_ATTACHMENT_TYPES_DENY=
# OPEN: dangerous types taken all the same, e.g. text/html or .svg (default: empty). They are still only ever
# sent as downloads (Content-Disposition: attachment, nosniff, a sandboxing CSP), never shown in the app.
CCMS_ATTACHMENT_TYPES_OPEN=

# Storage used (GET /storage-usage, administrators): uploaded media (images and attachments) and the archived
# release PDFs count; the Git content and the database are shown for information only.
# LIMIT_BYTES: the most bytes media and archived PDFs may hold together. An upload that would go past it is
# refused (409 storage-limit-reached) and nothing is stored; release PDFs are never refused. The admin view
# warns from 80 %. A change is audited (storage.limit-change) at the next start. Whole number of bytes from 1
# to 9007199254740991, e.g. 53687091200 for 50 GiB (default: unset, no limit).
CCMS_STORAGE_LIMIT_BYTES=
# RECOUNT_HOURS: how often the totals (kept up to date on every upload and delete) are counted afresh from the
# blob store and the database, which corrects any drift. Whole number from 1 to 8760 (default: 24).
CCMS_STORAGE_RECOUNT_HOURS=

# Image renditions (GET /assets/:hash?width=320|640|1280): WebPs made on first request with sharp and kept in
# the blob store. Only PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP are decoded (every other libvips loader is blocked).
# MAX_PIXELS: the most pixels (width x height) a source may have; a larger one is 422 too-large, refused from its
# header before decoding. Whole number from 1 to 268402689 (default: 40000000).
CCMS_RENDITION_MAX_PIXELS=
# TIMEOUT_MS: how long making one rendition may take, in milliseconds; past it 422 unprocessable-image.
# Whole number from 100 to 120000 (default: 10000).
CCMS_RENDITION_TIMEOUT_MS=
# CONCURRENCY: how many renditions one server makes at once; four times as many requests wait, more are
# 503 rendition-busy. Whole number from 1 to 32 (default: 2).
CCMS_RENDITION_CONCURRENCY=
# MAX_SOURCE_BYTES: the largest file a rendition is made of, in bytes; a larger one is 422 too-large.
# Whole number from 1 to 1073741824 (default: 52428800, 50 MiB).
CCMS_RENDITION_MAX_SOURCE_BYTES=

# Tests only (backend/api): an S3-compatible service the blob store's contract tests also run against
# (src/blobs/repos/blob-stores.spec.ts), e.g. the compose one, http://127.0.0.1:8333. Each run creates and
# deletes a openfolia-test-* bucket of its own. Unset (the default): those tests are skipped.
CCMS_TEST_S3_ENDPOINT=
# Tests only: credentials for CCMS_TEST_S3_ENDPOINT (default: the compose service's, ccms / ccms-local-secret)
# and its region (default: us-east-1).
CCMS_TEST_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CCMS_TEST_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
CCMS_TEST_S3_REGION=

# Notifications (GET /me/notifications): the fan-out reads the outbox every so many milliseconds, and at
# start-up. Whole number from 0 to 3600000 (default: 3000); 0 = not on a timer (tests run it themselves).
CCMS_NOTIFICATIONS_POLL_MS=
# Read notifications older than this many days are deleted (hourly); unread ones are kept.
# Whole number from 1 to 36500 (default: 90).
CCMS_NOTIFICATIONS_KEEP_DAYS=

# The instance secret key (#470; backend/api/README.md, "Secrets"): seals (AES-256-GCM) every secret the
# server stores and must use itself, such as webhook signing secrets. Never stored in the database, so a
# database dump alone opens nothing; never logged, never answered by the API.
# Leave all of these unset for a single server: on its first start the API makes a key file (below) and
# reads it on every later start. BACK UP THE KEY FILE: without it the stored secrets cannot be read, and
# the API refuses to start while the database holds secrets it cannot open (it never makes a new key then).
# Optional: the key itself, 32 random bytes as base64 (44 characters) or 64 hex digits, e.g.
# `openssl rand -base64 32`. Set it (the same on every server) for several API servers or a hosted setup,
# or from a secret store; then no key file is read or written. Default: unset.
CCMS_SECRET_KEY=
# Deprecated: the old name of CCMS_SECRET_KEY (#42), still read when CCMS_SECRET_KEY is unset (a warning
# at start-up). Set both only to the same key. Rename it to CCMS_SECRET_KEY. Default: unset.
CCMS_WEBHOOKS_SECRET_KEY=
# Where the key file is, when no variable sets the key: an absolute path. It holds the key as base64 and
# a newline; the API makes it with mode 0600 (its folder with 0700 when missing). Several servers on one
# machine or a shared volume may share it (they never make two keys). Default: ccms-secret.key in the
# folder that holds CCMS_CONTENT_DIR (for /srv/ccms/content.git: /srv/ccms/ccms-secret.key), beside the
# content repository you back up anyway, never inside it.
CCMS_SECRET_KEY_FILE=
# Whether the API makes the key file on its first start when there is none: true or false (default:
# true). false for hosted setups, where a missing key must not be made up: with no key set and no key
# file the API starts with webhooks off (404 not-configured; the editor says so), or refuses to start when
# the database already holds sealed secrets. A key file put there by the operator is still read.
CCMS_SECRET_KEY_GENERATE=
# Read only by `pnpm nx run api:rotate-secret-key` (stop every server first): the new key, same format as
# CCMS_SECRET_KEY. Required when CCMS_SECRET_KEY sets the key (set CCMS_SECRET_KEY to it afterwards);
# for the key file a new key is made when unset. Default: unset. Never leave it set.
CCMS_SECRET_KEY_NEW=

# Webhooks (POST /webhooks; #42); their signing secrets are sealed under the instance secret key above.
# How often the webhooks read the outbox for new events, in milliseconds, and at start-up.
# Whole number from 0 to 3600000 (default: 3000); 0 = not on a timer (tests run it themselves).
CCMS_WEBHOOKS_POLL_MS=
# One delivery attempt's whole time (resolving, connecting, sending, the answer's status line), in
# milliseconds; range 1000-60000 (default: 10000). Past it the attempt fails and is retried.
CCMS_WEBHOOKS_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Settled deliveries (succeeded, failed, skipped) older than this many days are deleted (hourly).
# Whole number from 1 to 3650 (default: 30).
CCMS_WEBHOOKS_KEEP_DAYS=
# Local testing only: true also allows http:// subscriber URLs (default: false, https only).
CCMS_WEBHOOKS_ALLOW_HTTP=
# Local testing only: true also allows URLs whose host is or resolves to a private, loopback, link-local
# or otherwise non-public address, and localhost (default: false). Never in a deployment: it opens the
# server to request forgery against its own network.
CCMS_WEBHOOKS_ALLOW_PRIVATE=

# Email (#609; deploy/README.md, "Email"): branded email through your own mail server (SMTP), in the
# person's language. Off while CCMS_MAIL_URL is unset: whatever would be emailed (a sign-in link) is
# offered as a link to copy instead. A queued email's details are sealed under the instance secret key
# above, so email also needs that key; without one it stays off (Admin, System, Email says why). Shown
# read-only in Admin, System, Email (never the user or the password), with "Send a test email".
# The mail server: smtp://host[:port] (STARTTLS, port 587 by default) or smtps://host[:port] (TLS from the
# start, port 465 by default). No user, password, path or query in it. Default: unset (no email).
CCMS_MAIL_URL=
# The user name to sign in to the mail server with (SMTP AUTH), one line. Default: unset (no sign-in).
CCMS_MAIL_USER=
# Its password (1 to 1024 characters). Never logged or shown. Default: unset. Required with CCMS_MAIL_USER,
# unless CCMS_MAIL_PASSWORD_FILE is set.
CCMS_MAIL_PASSWORD=
# A file holding the password (an absolute path, e.g. a Compose secret under /run/secrets/), read at
# start-up; its final line break is dropped. Wins over CCMS_MAIL_PASSWORD. Default: unset.
CCMS_MAIL_PASSWORD_FILE=
# The sender's address, bare (docs@example.com, no name: the sender's name is the branding's product
# name). Required with CCMS_MAIL_URL. Default: unset.
CCMS_MAIL_FROM=
# On smtp://: true refuses to send unless the server upgrades the connection with STARTTLS, so nothing
# (sign-in, addresses, links) crosses the network in plain text; false uses STARTTLS when offered.
# true or false (default: true). smtps:// always uses TLS. The certificate is always verified.
CCMS_MAIL_REQUIRE_TLS=
# A PEM file of certificate authorities to trust for the mail server, in place of the system's: for a
# mail server whose certificate a private authority signed. An absolute path. Default: unset.
CCMS_MAIL_CA_FILE=
# The language of an email to someone whose language is not known: en or de (default: en).
CCMS_MAIL_LANGUAGE=

# Audit log sink and retention (#379; backend/api/README.md, "Audit log"; deploy/README.md). Operator
# settings, read at start; the sink and retention run in a worker or all process (CCMS_ROLE).
# Where the audit log is copied to as it grows, every event at least once, in order (receivers dedupe
# by the event's id): https://host[:port]/path (each batch of up to 100 events POSTed as JSON, signed
# like a webhook) or syslog+tls://host[:port] (RFC 5425 over TLS, port 6514 by default). No credentials
# in the URL. A sink set on an installation with history sends the whole log first. Default: unset (no sink).
CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_URL=
# The https:// sink's signing secret: whsec_ and 64 lowercase hex digits (`openssl rand -hex 32`, then
# whsec_ in front). Required with an https:// URL; unused with syslog. Never logged. Or
# CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_SECRET_FILE (below). Default: unset.
CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_SECRET=
# Certificates (PEM) to trust for the sink instead of the system's, for a private CA: an absolute path,
# read at start (a missing file stops it). The sink's certificate is always checked. Default: unset.
CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_CA_FILE=
# How often new events are delivered, in milliseconds, and at start-up. After a failed delivery the next
# waits 30 s, doubling to 10 min, until one succeeds. Whole number from 0 to 3600000 (default: 3000);
# 0 = not on a timer (tests run it themselves).
CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_POLL_MS=
# One delivery's whole time (connecting, TLS, sending, the answer's status line), in milliseconds;
# range 1000-60000 (default: 10000). Past it the delivery fails and is tried again.
CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Retention: audit events recorded more than this many days ago are removed (at start-up and daily),
# each removal recorded as an audit-log.prune event; with a sink set, never one it has not sent yet.
# Whole number from 1 to 36500. Default: unset (kept for ever).
CCMS_AUDIT_KEEP_DAYS=

# Backups (#529; deploy/README.md, "Backups"): the backup service (`CCMS_ROLE=backup`, the backup image)
# backs up the database, the content repository, the blobs and the instance secret key, encrypted (age)
# to the backup key, and checks each backup. Set it up in the editor (Admin, Backups); nothing below is
# needed. Precedence: a CCMS_BACKUP_* variable below, when set, wins over the page and shows read-only
# there, naming the variable; unset, the page's value counts (stored in the database, read at every pass,
# no restart); unset on both, the default given. The service reads the database and the instance secret
# key settings above, CCMS_CONTENT_DIR and CCMS_BLOB_* (with CCMS_BLOB_DRIVER=s3 the blobs stay in their
# bucket, not in the backup: keep that bucket versioned).
# Read by the API too: a last good backup older than this many hours shows a warning in Admin and tells
# the admin.backups holders once. Whole number from 1 to 8760 (default: 26).
CCMS_BACKUP_WARN_AFTER_HOURS=
# Read by the backup service only, from here on.
# The backup volume: local backups (in a subfolder of it, set in the page). An absolute path
# (default: /backups; the backup image sets it).
CCMS_BACKUP_DIR=
# Where a run stages its unencrypted parts (the dump, the bundle, a check's unpacked copy) while it lasts:
# an absolute path to an existing folder owned by the service's user with mode 0700, no symbolic link, and
# neither inside nor around CCMS_BACKUP_DIR (copied off the host) or the instance's data; refused otherwise.
# Each run and restore gets a private folder in it, and what a stopped one left is removed at the next start
# (only those folders: nothing else in it is touched). Needs about twice the size of a backup free during a
# run. Default: unset, a fresh private folder in the system's temporary folder for each start of the
# service; the backup image sets /staging, the backup-staging volume of deploy/compose.yaml.
CCMS_BACKUP_STAGING_DIR=
# How often the service looks for "Back up now", "Test location" and due runs, in milliseconds.
# Whole number from 1000 to 600000 (default: 5000).
CCMS_BACKUP_POLL_MS=
# Where the check makes its throwaway database (restored from the dump, then dropped; leftovers older than
# an hour are dropped at start): a Postgres URL like CCMS_DATABASE_URL whose user may CREATEDB. It needs
# about as much free disk as the database. Default: the instance's own server (CCMS_DATABASE_URL).
CCMS_BACKUP_VERIFY_DATABASE_URL=
# Backups on or off: true or false. Default: unset (the page; off until it is turned on).
CCMS_BACKUP_ENABLED=
# When to back up: a five-field cron expression (minute hour day month weekday), e.g. "0 2 * * *".
# Fixes the page's frequency and time. Default: unset (the page; daily at 02:00).
CCMS_BACKUP_SCHEDULE=
# The time zone the schedule and retention read days in: an IANA name, e.g. Europe/Berlin.
# Default: unset (the page; UTC).
CCMS_BACKUP_TIME_ZONE=
# Retention: how many daily, weekly and monthly backups are kept (the newest of each day, ISO week and
# month); the newest backup is always kept. Whole numbers (daily 0-366, weekly 0-520, monthly 0-1200).
# Default: unset (the page; 7, 4 and 12).
CCMS_BACKUP_RETENTION_DAILY=
CCMS_BACKUP_RETENTION_WEEKLY=
CCMS_BACKUP_RETENTION_MONTHLY=
# Where backups go: local (a subfolder of CCMS_BACKUP_DIR) or s3 (an S3-compatible bucket). Setting it
# fixes the whole location, with the variables below. Default: unset (the page; local, the volume's root).
CCMS_BACKUP_LOCATION=
# With local: the subfolder of CCMS_BACKUP_DIR, relative, e.g. nightly (default: empty, the root).
CCMS_BACKUP_LOCAL_SUBFOLDER=
# With s3: the endpoint URL (unset for AWS itself), the region (default: us-east-1), the bucket
# (required), a key prefix such as nightly/ (default: empty), and the access key (both required; each
# may come from <NAME>_FILE). Never logged or answered.
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_REGION=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_PREFIX=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Lets the backup service reach an S3 endpoint on a private or loopback address (an S3 server on the same
# network, e.g. MinIO beside the stack): true or false. Every connection resolves the endpoint's host and
# refuses it when any address it resolves to is private or loopback without this, and always when it is
# link-local or a cloud metadata address (169.254.0.0/16, fe80::/10, fd00:ec2::254, in any IPv6 spelling).
# Default: false.
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_ALLOW_PRIVATE=
# Check each backup after it is made: true or false. Default: unset (the page; true).
CCMS_BACKUP_VERIFY=
# How it is checked: true decrypts the finished backup with the key the server keeps sealed; false keeps
# no key on the server and checks the parts before they are encrypted, then the encrypted file by size
# and SHA-256 (deploy/README.md, "Backups"). Default: unset (the page; true).
CCMS_BACKUP_VERIFY_BY_DECRYPTING=
# The backup key from a file instead of the page: an absolute path to an age identity file (age-keygen
# writes one). Backups are encrypted to its public key; `backup restore` reads it as the default key.
# Default: unset (the page makes the key and keeps only its public half, and the private half sealed for
# the check).
CCMS_BACKUP_KEY_FILE=

# Background jobs (pg-boss, in the schema pgboss of CCMS_DATABASE_URL's database; installed and upgraded with the
# migrations). Each job queue is polled every so many milliseconds: 0, or a whole number from 500 to 3600000
# (default: 2000). 0 = this server runs no jobs and only enqueues them (tests run them themselves; a deployment may
# leave the work to other servers, or set CCMS_ROLE=api, which also stops the background loops).
CCMS_JOBS_POLL_MS=
# Most connections of the job queue's own pool, beside CCMS_DATABASE_POOL_MAX; whole number 1-100 (default: 4).
CCMS_JOBS_POOL_MAX=

# Imports (POST /imports, #256): an uploaded bundle is checked, then applied into a change set by a background job.
# The largest upload, in bytes; a larger one is 422 too-large and reading stops there.
# Whole number from 1 to 1073741824 (default: 67108864, 64 MiB). The upload is held in memory while it is checked.
CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_BYTES=
# The most entries (files and folders) an import archive may hold; whole number 1-65534 (default: 5000).
CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_FILES=
# The most bytes an archive's files may hold together unpacked (decompression bombs are refused against it before
# anything is unpacked); whole number from 1 to 2147483647 (default: 268435456, 256 MiB). Held in memory while checked.
CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_UNPACKED_BYTES=
# The most folders deep a path in an import archive may lie; whole number 1-64 (default: 4; assets/<hash> lies in 1).
CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_PATH_DEPTH=
# The deepest nesting of arrays and objects in import.json; whole number 16-256 (default: 128).
CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_JSON_DEPTH=
# The largest import.json an import reads, in bytes, refused before it is parsed (parsing takes up to about 80 times
# its size in memory, and two checks and one apply job may run at once); whole number from 1 to 33554432
# (default: 8388608, 8 MiB; at the most, a check may take about 2 GB). A document with more than 1,000,000 values is refused before it is checked.
CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES=
# A DITA import's conversion runs in a child process of its own (#432): its heap in MiB (whole number 64-16384,
# default: 1024) and its longest time in milliseconds (whole number 1000-3600000, default: 120000). Past either, the
# import is refused as 422 import-too-large (meta.reason memory, timeout, or size: an import.json past
# CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES, refused in the child so the server never receives it); the server is unharmed. The
# bound is the JavaScript heap: the archive's unpacked files (up to CCMS_IMPORT_MAX_UNPACKED_BYTES) come on top, and the
# answer (import.json and the assets) about twice while it is sent, so a child takes up to about the heap plus twice
# the unpacked bytes; the server itself holds about three times the unpacked bytes per running conversion (the
# archive, the request and the answer). Two checks and, with CCMS_ROLE=all, one apply job may each run one, so plan
# room for three.
CCMS_IMPORT_CONVERT_MAX_MEMORY_MB=
CCMS_IMPORT_CONVERT_TIMEOUT_MS=
# How an import is cut into save points: the most modules and manuals per commit (whole number 1-1000, default 1000)
# and the most bytes of working copies per commit (whole number 1-33554432, default 33554432, 32 MiB). A larger import
# becomes several commits on one change set.
CCMS_IMPORT_COMMIT_FILES=
CCMS_IMPORT_COMMIT_BYTES=

# The largest ZIP of a release's files that GET /releases/:id/outputs/archive serves (#469), in bytes, ZIP headers
# included (whole number 1-4294967295, default 2147483648, 2 GiB; at most 4 GiB less one byte, as no ZIP64 is written).
# A larger one is refused with 422 release-archive-too-large; its files still download one by one. Also the largest
# offline package (#59) a release's job builds: a larger one fails with offline-package-too-large.
CCMS_RELEASE_ARCHIVE_MAX_BYTES=

# Whether each release gets its offline packages (#59): a ZIP per configured language and audience level (up to the
# highest any manual has), its manuals as HTML pages and PDFs, that opens from the file system without a network.
# Built by the release's output jobs once its PDFs are done, kept in the blob store, listed with the release's files
# (GET /releases/:id/outputs?filter[kind]=offline-package). true or false (default true).
CCMS_OFFLINE_PACKAGES=

# Package downloads (#654): iiRDS (GET /releases/:id/iirds-packages/:packageId/file) and DITA
# (GET /releases/:id/dita-packages/:packageId/file). The server sends at most 4 of each kind at once; past that, or past
# a reader's share, 429 rate-limited before any of the file is sent. These settings apply to both kinds.
# A download no byte of which is read for this long is cut, freeing its turn (milliseconds, 1000-3600000, default 60000).
CCMS_PACKAGE_SEND_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=
# A download still going after this long is cut (milliseconds, 1000-86400000, default 1800000, half an hour).
CCMS_PACKAGE_SEND_TIMEOUT_MS=
# A download read more slowly than this on average, once its first idle timeout has passed, is cut (bytes a second,
# whole number 1-1073741824, default 16384).
CCMS_PACKAGE_SEND_MIN_BYTES_PER_SECOND=
# How many of those 4 one reader may hold at once, per kind; past it 429 rate-limited (whole number 1-3, default 1;
# at most 3, so one reader never holds every turn).
CCMS_PACKAGE_SENDS_PER_ACTOR=
# Deprecated: the old names of the four settings above (#433, from when they bounded the DITA downloads only), with the
# same formats (CCMS_DITA_SENDS_PER_ACTOR is now 1-3 as well; it was 1-4). Still read when the new name is unset (a
# warning at start-up); set beside it, each must hold the same value. Rename them to CCMS_PACKAGE_SEND_*. Default: unset.
CCMS_DITA_SEND_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=
CCMS_DITA_SEND_TIMEOUT_MS=
CCMS_DITA_SEND_MIN_BYTES_PER_SECOND=
CCMS_DITA_SENDS_PER_ACTOR=

# The most outputs one release plans (#477): every manual at its tag, in each of its variants and each configured
# language, and its offline packages (#59) (whole number 1-1000000, default 20000). A release with more gets none: its planning is recorded as refused
# (meta.outputs of GET /releases/:id: state failed, refused.reason too-many-outputs) and logged once, and
# POST /releases/:id/outputs/plan answers 422 too-many-outputs until the limit is raised.
CCMS_RELEASE_MAX_OUTPUTS=

# Model-based style review (POST /change-sets/:id/modules/:lang/:moduleId/style-review), off by default: with
# CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_URL unset the route answers 404 not-configured and nothing is ever sent anywhere. When set, a
# module's translatable text and the style guide in openfolia.yaml (styleGuide) are posted to this endpoint, and only when
# an author asks for a review. Any chat-completions style HTTP endpoint, hosted or self-hosted: the full URL a request
# is posted to (http:// or https://, no credentials, query or fragment; https:// required when an API key is set,
# except to localhost / 127.x / [::1]). Default: unset (off).
CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_URL=
# Sent as "Authorization: Bearer <key>"; optional (a self-hosted model may need none). Never logged or audited.
CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_API_KEY=
# The model name the endpoint expects (the request's "model"); required when CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_URL is set.
CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_MODEL=
# Reviews one person may ask for per minute, on each server (more: 429 with Retry-After); whole number 1-600 (default: 6).
CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_PER_MINUTE=
# How long one review may take in milliseconds before the request is cut off (503 style-review-timeout with
# Retry-After); range 1000-300000 (default: 30000).
CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MS=

# PDF rendering. Worker processes compiling PDFs; range 1-64 (default: one per spare CPU, at most 64; with
# CCMS_ROLE=api at most 2, for readers' PDFs only). They start with the first PDF. About 450 MB each at most.
CCMS_PDF_WORKERS=
# PDF jobs allowed to wait for a free worker before requests get 503; range 0-10000 (default: 4 per worker; 0 = never wait).
CCMS_PDF_QUEUE=
# Deadline for one PDF in milliseconds, waiting included, up to 86400000 (default: 60000).
CCMS_PDF_TIMEOUT_MS=
# Memory one PDF worker process may use, in MiB (its resident memory, the compiler's included):
# past it the process is stopped and that PDF fails (422 render-memory-exceeded), so a page design
# template that exhausts memory stops there. Range 256-65536 (default: 2048).
CCMS_PDF_MEMORY_MB=
# Release files (one PDF per manual, variant and language) one server renders at once, in the
# background on the same PDF workers; a reader's PDF or preview waiting for a worker goes ahead of
# them (one already rendering finishes first, so keep this below the workers to leave readers one).
# Range 1 to the PDF workers (CCMS_PDF_WORKERS, else one per spare CPU); default: half the PDF
# workers, at least 1; with CCMS_ROLE=worker, which serves no readers, all of them.
CCMS_RENDER_CONCURRENCY=

# Editor dev server (frontend/editor/proxy.conf.mjs): proxies /api to the API and adds the bearer
# token (CCMS_API_TOKEN above) itself, so the token never reaches the browser. Address of the API
# (default: http://127.0.0.1:<PORT in .env.local>, else port 3100). The dev server's own PORT in the
# environment is never used for this: set CCMS_API_URL to reach an API on another port.
CCMS_API_URL=

# MCP server (backend/mcp, #53): agents read the released content through it. Read from the
# environment of the process that starts it (a desktop assistant's MCP config, or the shell), not
# by the API. Base URL of the content API (http or https; e.g. http://127.0.0.1:3100). Required.
CCMS_MCP_API_URL=
# A service account token (ccms_sat_…) whose roles hold content.read alone (`pnpm nx run
# api:service-token -- <account> --role <role>`); the server refuses to answer with a wider one.
# Required. Its scope is what every tool sees.
CCMS_MCP_API_TOKEN=
# Streamable HTTP transport (`openfolia-mcp --http`) only. Address to listen on (default: 127.0.0.1;
# anything else is reachable from other machines: put TLS in front of it).
CCMS_MCP_HTTP_HOST=
# Port to listen on, 0-65535 (default: 3200; 0 picks a free one). The endpoint is /mcp.
CCMS_MCP_HTTP_PORT=
# Bearer token HTTP callers send (Authorization: Bearer …). Must come from a random generator
# (`openssl rand -hex 32`, 256 bits): a typed one is unsafe even when accepted. At least 32
# characters, 12 different ones, no repeated pattern, not CCMS_MCP_API_TOKEN. Required for --http.
CCMS_MCP_HTTP_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated Origins a browser-based caller may send (e.g. https://assistant.example); any
# other Origin header is 403 (DNS rebinding). Default: none, which only non-browser clients pass.
CCMS_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Embedding worker (backend/embedder, deploy/compose.embedder.yaml, #532): a sentence-embedding model on the CPU
# that the API's CCMS_EMBEDDER_URL can point at, so semantic search runs without text leaving the installation.
# Read by the worker's process, not by the API; with compose.embedder.yaml, Compose reads them from deploy/.env.
# The worker also reads CCMS_EMBEDDER_MODEL (above: the name the API sends; a request naming another is refused)
# and CCMS_EMBEDDER_DIMENSIONS (above: checked against the model's vectors as it loads; at most 2000). It makes
# no network call: the model is a folder a person fills once (deploy/README.md, "Semantic search").
# The folder holding the model: model.onnx and tokenizer.json (default: /models, where the image mounts it).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_MODEL_DIR=
# The SHA-256 of model.onnx and of tokenizer.json, 64 hexadecimal digits each (sha256sum <file>). Required: a
# file whose checksum differs is refused and the worker does not start.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_MODEL_SHA256=
CCMS_EMBEDDER_TOKENIZER_SHA256=
# How a text's token vectors become one, as the model's card says: mean (default) or cls (the first token's).
# Unused for a model that answers one vector per text itself (an output named sentence_embedding).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_POOLING=
# Text put before every input, for a model that expects one (e.g. "query: "); at most 100 characters (default:
# none).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_PREFIX=
# The most tokens of one text the model reads; the rest is cut. Whole number 8-2048 (default: the tokenizer's
# own truncation length, else 512).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_MAX_TOKENS=
# CPU threads one model run uses, 1-64 (default: 2). One request runs at a time.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_THREADS=
# Requests that may wait while one runs, 0-64 (default: 8); one more is answered 503 with Retry-After. Open
# connections are limited to this plus 8; one more is closed at once.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_QUEUE=
# The address and port the worker listens on (default: 127.0.0.1 and 8090; the image: 0.0.0.0, on its internal
# network only). It has no authentication: never publish it. Port 0-65535 (0: a free one).
CCMS_EMBEDDER_HOST=
CCMS_EMBEDDER_PORT=
# Tests only (backend/embedder/README.md, "Testing with a real model"): a model folder, its dimensions and an
# optional prefix for the opt-in test with a real model. Unset: that test is skipped.
CCMS_EMBEDDER_TEST_MODEL_DIR=
CCMS_EMBEDDER_TEST_DIMENSIONS=
CCMS_EMBEDDER_TEST_PREFIX=
# Tracker connector (connectors/tracker, #141): imports items of an issue tracker through the import
# API into a change set for review. Read from the environment of the process that runs it (the
# shell, cron), not by the API. Base URL of the content API: https, or http to this machine only
# (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:3100). Required. The connector calls nothing else.
CCMS_CONNECTOR_API_URL=
# Path of the cookie file of a signed-in person who may import (admin.roles and content.edit),
# as curl writes it when signing in (`curl -c cookies.txt …`, the import format's guide, "Sign in
# for the import"). Readable by its owner alone (chmod 600), else refused; read again on every run,
# so signing in again renews it. Required.
CCMS_CONNECTOR_SESSION_FILE=
# The secret the source signs its triggers with, when the connector runs with --listen (a signed
# POST /trigger starts a run: HMAC-SHA256 over `<unix seconds>.<body>`, header
# X-Openfolia-Signature). At least 32 characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; the source holds the
# same value. Required with --listen, unused without. Never printed.
CCMS_CONNECTOR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Container deployment (deploy/compose.yaml, the guide in deploy/README.md). Compose reads these from the
# environment or from deploy/.env (beside compose.yaml); any API setting above goes into deploy/api.env
# instead, except those compose.yaml sets itself (CCMS_AUTH_MODE, CCMS_API_TOKEN, CCMS_EDITOR_ORIGINS,
# CCMS_SOURCE_URL, CCMS_PUBLIC_URL, CCMS_FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL, CCMS_FIRST_ADMIN_NAME, CCMS_FIRST_ADMIN_LINK_LOG, CCMS_TRUST_PROXY (default 1 there: the editor's nginx), CCMS_MAIL_* (email): set those here; CCMS_DATABASE_URL it builds from POSTGRES_PASSWORD). The images set HOST=0.0.0.0, PORT=3000,
# CCMS_CONTENT_DIR=/data/content.git, CCMS_BLOB_DRIVER=fs and CCMS_BLOB_FS_ROOT=/data/blobs themselves.
# Postgres's password, also put into the API's CCMS_DATABASE_URL. Required, no default. Letters and digits only
# (it goes into a URL), e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`. Read by Postgres on the first start only: changing it later
# needs ALTER USER in the database too.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Where the images come from: the registry path before /api, /backup, /editor and /mcp, e.g. ghcr.io/<owner>/openfolia
# for the public images (default: openfolia, the names compose.build.yaml builds locally).
OPENFOLIA_IMAGES=
# The image tag: a release (v1.2.3), latest (the newest release), main, or a commit SHA of main (default: local,
# what compose.build.yaml builds).
OPENFOLIA_VERSION=
# The API's settings file beside compose.yaml (default: ./api.env, read when it exists); the smoke test sets
# /dev/null so it never reads a deployment's. The workers read it too.
OPENFOLIA_API_ENV_FILE=
# The workers' own settings file beside compose.yaml, read over the API's (default: ./worker.env, read when it
# exists), e.g. CCMS_PDF_WORKERS and CCMS_RENDER_CONCURRENCY for the workers only (#527).
OPENFOLIA_WORKER_ENV_FILE=
# The CPU limit of each worker container, in CPUs, e.g. 2 (default: 0, no limit). At most the host's CPUs: Docker
# refuses to start a container with more. Set CCMS_PDF_WORKERS in worker.env to match it: the PDF pool's default
# is the host's CPUs less one, not the limit's, and a worker renders on all its PDF workers.
OPENFOLIA_WORKER_CPUS=
# The api service's CCMS_ROLE (default: api, the worker service runs the jobs). all runs everything in the api
# container instead; then start with --scale worker=0.
OPENFOLIA_API_ROLE=
# The backup service's settings file beside compose.yaml, read after api.env (default: ./backup.env, read when
# it exists): the CCMS_BACKUP_* settings above. The smoke test sets /dev/null.
OPENFOLIA_BACKUP_ENV_FILE=
# The address the published ports listen on (default: 127.0.0.1, for a reverse proxy on the same machine;
# 0.0.0.0 publishes them to every network, plain HTTP included, past ufw/firewalld rules: then only on a network
# you trust, with TLS in front for everyone else).
OPENFOLIA_BIND=
# The address the API's own published port listens on (default: 127.0.0.1, whatever OPENFOLIA_BIND says). Readers
# and clients reach the API through the editor (/api/, /d/). Publishing this port wider lets anyone who reaches it
# name their own address to CCMS_TRUST_PROXY's hop count (deploy/README.md, "Reverse proxy with TLS"): then set
# CCMS_TRUST_PROXY=none, and raise or turn off CCMS_DELIVERY_PER_MINUTE (every reader through the editor shares one
# budget then, and one failed-sign-in window).
OPENFOLIA_API_BIND=
# The embedding worker (compose.embedder.yaml): the folder with the model's files, mounted read-only at /models
# (default: ./embedder-model beside compose.yaml), its memory limit (default: 2g; the model's file size about twice
# while it loads, plus one request's working memory) and its CPU limit in CPUs (default: 0, no limit; at most the
# host's CPUs). Set CCMS_EMBEDDER_THREADS to match a limit.
OPENFOLIA_EMBEDDER_MODEL_DIR=
OPENFOLIA_EMBEDDER_MEMORY=
OPENFOLIA_EMBEDDER_CPUS=
# The published ports of the editor (default: 8080), the API (default: 3000) and the MCP server (default: 3200;
# only with `--profile mcp`). Whole numbers 1-65535.
OPENFOLIA_EDITOR_PORT=
OPENFOLIA_API_PORT=
OPENFOLIA_MCP_PORT=

# The editor image (its web server, deploy/docker/editor/): the port it listens on inside the container
# (default: 8080) and the API's address, http(s)://host[:port] without a path (default: http://api:3000, the
# compose service). It serves the editor and proxies /api to that address, looking the host up through the
# container's DNS resolver every 10 s (never /etc/hosts: use a DNS name or an IP address).
CCMS_EDITOR_PORT=
CCMS_EDITOR_API_URL=
# The host names the editor answers for, comma-separated host[:port] (the port is not compared), e.g.
# docs.example.com,127.0.0.1. Any other Host gets 421 from a default server and is never proxied (DNS rebinding).
# Required with CCMS_EDITOR_API_TOKEN. Default: unset, any Host.
CCMS_EDITOR_HOSTS=
# Optional: a token the editor's proxy adds to /api requests (32-512 characters of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ ~ + / = -),
# replacing any the browser sent. Only for CCMS_EDITOR_HOSTS, and only for requests from the editor's own page (its
# Origin, or Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, which browsers send only over HTTPS or to localhost: so open such an
# editor over HTTPS or on localhost); anything else is refused. For a demo instance only (with
# CCMS_AUTH_MODE=demo and the same CCMS_API_TOKEN): anyone who reaches the editor then acts with it, so keep it on
# a private network (deploy/README.md, "Signing in"). Default: unset, the browser's own Authorization is passed on.
CCMS_EDITOR_API_TOKEN=
# Instead of CCMS_EDITOR_API_TOKEN: the path of a file holding it, e.g. a Compose secret /run/secrets/editor-token
# (default: unset). Setting both is refused.
CCMS_EDITOR_API_TOKEN_FILE=

# Secrets from files (the API, backup and MCP images' entrypoint, deploy/docker/node-entrypoint.sh): the path of a
# file holding the value, e.g. a Compose secret under /run/secrets/, instead of the value itself; trailing
# newlines are dropped. Setting a value and its _FILE is refused. Default: unset. (The instance secret key has
# its own CCMS_SECRET_KEY_FILE above, which the API reads itself.)
CCMS_DATABASE_URL_FILE=
CCMS_API_TOKEN_FILE=
CCMS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID_FILE=
CCMS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_FILE=
CCMS_STYLE_REVIEW_API_KEY_FILE=
CCMS_EMBEDDER_API_KEY_FILE=
CCMS_AUDIT_SINK_SECRET_FILE=
CCMS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=
CCMS_MCP_API_TOKEN_FILE=
CCMS_MCP_HTTP_TOKEN_FILE=
CCMS_BACKUP_VERIFY_DATABASE_URL_FILE=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID_FILE=
CCMS_BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_FILE=

# The smoke test (deploy/smoke-test.sh), read from the shell: the Compose project (default: openfolia-smoke),
# the ports it publishes on 127.0.0.1 for the API, the editor and the MCP server (defaults: 3103, 4303 and 3203), 0 to use the images as they are instead of
# building them (default: 1), 1 to leave the stack running (default: 0), and a path to copy the rendered PDF to
# (default: none).
SMOKE_PROJECT=
SMOKE_API_PORT=
SMOKE_EDITOR_PORT=
SMOKE_MCP_PORT=
SMOKE_BUILD=
SMOKE_KEEP=
SMOKE_PDF_OUT=

# The one-command self-host (deploy/self-host.sh, #373), read from the shell: the settings file it makes when
# missing and Compose reads (default: deploy/.env beside compose.yaml), and how long it waits for the services to
# be healthy, in seconds (default: 300).
OPENFOLIA_ENV_FILE=
OPENFOLIA_WAIT_TIMEOUT=

# Its test (deploy/self-host-test.sh), read from the shell: the Compose project (default: openfolia-self-host),
# the ports it publishes on 127.0.0.1 for the API, the editor and the test OpenID Connect provider (defaults: 3104,
# 4304 and 9404), and 1 to leave the stack running (default: 0). The test provider (deploy/smoke-oidc.yaml) reads
# SMOKE_OIDC_PORT (its port, default 9404) and SMOKE_ADMIN_EMAIL (the address of its one login, admin; default
# admin@example.com), which the test sets.
SELF_HOST_PROJECT=
SELF_HOST_API_PORT=
SELF_HOST_EDITOR_PORT=
SELF_HOST_OIDC_PORT=
SELF_HOST_KEEP=
SMOKE_OIDC_PORT=
SMOKE_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# The test of the images pinned by their digests (deploy/digests-test.sh, #739), read from the shell: the port of
# the registry of its own it starts on 127.0.0.1 (default: 5739).
DIGESTS_TEST_REGISTRY_PORT=

# Docs site (frontend/docs, `pnpm nx build docs`).
# Read from the build's environment, not from this file: the values are written into the static
# site, so set them for the build of the site you publish.

# The API base URL the API reference's playground sends requests to, and the server its pages name. An
# absolute http(s) URL (default: http://localhost:3000, the container setup's API).
DOCS_API_BASE_URL=
# The docs site's own address, for the absolute links in /llms.txt and /llms-full.txt. An absolute http(s)
# URL without a trailing slash (default: http://localhost:3000).
DOCS_SITE_URL=
# The repository's web address: the GitHub link in the site's navigation, and links to files in it
# (for example the import format's guide). An absolute http(s) URL of a GitHub repository (default:
# https://github.com/openfolia/openfolia, the project's own; set it for a fork).
DOCS_REPOSITORY_URL=
# The release these docs belong to, as its tag names it: v1.2.3 (not a pre-release: only a release gets the
# files the guide downloads). The install guide for coding agents (/agents) pins it: the images it pulls and the
# compose file it downloads. Set it for the build of a release's docs; DOCS_SITE_URL must then be set, and it
# and DOCS_RELEASE_URL be https (plain http only on 127.0.0.1 or localhost, for a test). Default: unset, the development docs,
# whose guide pins no release and says so.
DOCS_RELEASE=
# Where the release's files (compose.yaml, compose.digests.yaml, SHA256SUMS) are downloaded from: an absolute URL, the folder that
# holds them, without query or fragment. Set only together with DOCS_RELEASE. Default: <DOCS_REPOSITORY_URL>/releases/download/<DOCS_RELEASE>, the GitHub Release.
DOCS_RELEASE_URL=
# The image repository the install guide pulls from, without a tag (registry[:port]/path, lowercase): each
# image is <DOCS_IMAGES>/<image>:<DOCS_RELEASE>. Default: ghcr.io/<owner>/openfolia, the owner of a GitHub
# DOCS_REPOSITORY_URL (else ghcr.io/openfolia/openfolia).
DOCS_IMAGES=
# The release's images by their digests (#739): the text of the images.lock the release workflow attaches to the
# release, one <DOCS_IMAGES>/<image>:<DOCS_RELEASE>@sha256:<digest> per line (or separated by spaces). The install
# guide pins every image by it: it names the SHA-256 of the release's compose.digests.yaml, which it downloads, and
# checks the running containers against the digests. Required for a release's docs (with DOCS_RELEASE), and set
# only together with it. Default: unset.
DOCS_RELEASE_DIGESTS=
# The release's signatures (#745), when the release workflow signed its images (repository variable SIGN_IMAGES):
# the text of the signatures.sha256 it attaches to the release, one "<sha256>  <file>" per line (or separated by
# spaces), for trusted_root.json and <image>.sigstore.json of every image. The install guide then names each file's
# SHA-256 and checks the images' signatures with cosign, offline, before pulling. Set only together with DOCS_RELEASE.
# Default: unset, the release is not signed and the guide says so.
DOCS_RELEASE_SIGNATURES=
# The identity the signatures must carry (cosign --certificate-identity): an https URL or an email, only letters,
# digits and . _ ~ : / % @ + -. Set only with DOCS_RELEASE_SIGNATURES. Default: the release workflow of the GitHub
# repository DOCS_REPOSITORY_URL at the release's tag,
# https://github.com/<owner>/<repository>/.github/workflows/images.yml@refs/tags/<DOCS_RELEASE>; required when
# DOCS_REPOSITORY_URL is not on github.com.
DOCS_RELEASE_SIGNER_IDENTITY=
# The OIDC issuer the signatures must carry (cosign --certificate-oidc-issuer): an https URL. Set only with
# DOCS_RELEASE_SIGNATURES. Default: https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com, GitHub Actions'.
DOCS_RELEASE_SIGNER_ISSUER=
# Where `pnpm docs:publish` (scripts/docs-publish.mjs) tags and pushes the docs site's image: an image repository
# without a tag (registry[:port]/path, lowercase). Read by that command only, not by the site's build. Default:
# ghcr.io/<owner>/openfolia-docs, the owner of a GitHub DOCS_REPOSITORY_URL (else ghcr.io/openfolia/openfolia-docs).
DOCS_PUBLISH_IMAGE=

# Portal (frontend/portal, `pnpm nx run portal:site`): one audience's static portal, a site per language.
# Read from the build's environment, not from this file. Keep the token out of files: set it in the build job's
# secret store. The build refuses a token that reads above the audience or may do more than read released content.

# The API's base URL. An absolute https URL; http only to this machine (127.0.0.1, localhost, [::1]). No user,
# password, query or fragment. Required.
CCMS_PORTAL_API_URL=
# A service account token (ccms_sat_<16 hex>_<64 hex>) whose roles hold only content.read, each with a maxAudience
# of at most CCMS_PORTAL_AUDIENCE (Admin -> Service accounts). Sent only in the Authorization header. Required.
CCMS_PORTAL_TOKEN=
# The audience level the portal is for (an audience ID of openfolia.yaml, e.g. public). Nothing above it reaches the
# site: one build per audience. Required.
CCMS_PORTAL_AUDIENCE=
# The languages to build, one site each: comma-separated language tags of openfolia.yaml (default: every configured
# language).
CCMS_PORTAL_LANGUAGES=
# The releases to build: comma-separated release IDs (UUIDs), none withdrawn (default: each product's newest
# release that is not withdrawn).
CCMS_PORTAL_RELEASES=
# Where the sites are written: <dir>/<lang>/ and <dir>/index.html; a path, relative to frontend/portal (default:
# dist). Replaced as a whole once every language is built.
CCMS_PORTAL_OUT_DIR=
# The path the sites are served under, starting and ending with "/" (default: /): each language at
# <path><lang>/.
CCMS_PORTAL_BASE_PATH=
# The organisation's branding (Admin -> Branding, the API's public GET /branding): its name, logos, favicon and
# colours on every page. `on` (default) or `off` for a neutral site with OpenFolia's default look. Without branding
# set, the site has the default look either way.
CCMS_PORTAL_BRANDING=
# The build sets CCMS_PORTAL_SNAPSHOT, CCMS_PORTAL_SITE_OUT and CCMS_PORTAL_SITE_BASE for Astro's own process (the
# snapshot file, the language's output folder, its path): not settings, never set by hand.

# Workflow scripts (scripts/, .githooks/). Read from the shell's environment, not from this file.

# Base branch for `pnpm review:diff` when no --base is given (e.g. origin/sprint-2; default: the
# agent slot's base, else origin/main); sync:main takes --base instead.
BASE_BRANCH=
# Set to 1 to skip the post-merge hook's `pnpm check:changed` (.githooks/post-merge) once.
SKIP_POST_MERGE_CHECK=
# Nx's own: `false` runs Nx without its daemon. An agent slot's settings set it (#615): in a
# worktree the daemon's watcher sees no edit, so it would hash tasks as the files were when it
# started. `pnpm check` sets it in any worktree unless given. Default (unset): the daemon runs.
NX_DAEMON=
# GitHub project board `pnpm merge:pr` moves closed issues to Done on: the owner (org or user)
# and the project number. `pnpm setup:board` writes them; gh needs the `project` scope.
GH_PROJECT_OWNER=
GH_PROJECT_NUMBER=

# Demo videos (scripts/demo/, docs/demo-videos.md). Read from the shell's environment, not from this file.

# The ffmpeg and ffprobe the assembly and the encodes run (default: those on the PATH).
FFMPEG=
FFPROBE=
# The ElevenLabs voice per language for a tab video's voice-over (`node scripts/demo/voice.mjs`): the ID of a
# voice in the account's voices (no default: the script refuses without one).
DEMO_VOICE_EN=
DEMO_VOICE_DE=
# The ElevenLabs API key. Never put it in this file or any other: voice.mjs asks for it without echo when it is not
# in the environment, and never writes or prints it.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# The ElevenLabs API's base URL, for a test against a local stub (default: https://api.elevenlabs.io).
ELEVENLABS_API_BASE=
# The hero's music (`node scripts/demo/assemble.mjs hero`): an audio file whose sting plays under the intro card
# and whose ending plays under the end card (default: none, no music). Check the track's licence first.
DEMO_MUSIC=
# Seconds into DEMO_MUSIC where the sting starts (default: 0).
DEMO_MUSIC_STING_FROM=
# Seconds into DEMO_MUSIC of its last hit, which lands on the end card's logo (default: half a second before its end).
DEMO_MUSIC_HIT=
# A tab video's music bed (`node scripts/demo/assemble.mjs <tab video>`): an audio file laid very quietly under the
# voice in the cut with sound, looped if shorter than the film (default: none, no bed). Never committed; check its licence.
DEMO_BED=
